  <section class="sec" id="faq" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> FAQ</span>
        <h2>Knowing when to hire, answered.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How many hours of admin work justify a full-time remote hire? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Once recurring delegable work passes roughly 15 to 20 hours a week, a dedicated full-time professional is usually cheaper per hour of output than hourly arrangements, and you gain continuity. Below 10 hours a week, part-time hourly support may fit better.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What role should I hire first? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">The role that removes the most recurring work from the most expensive person. For most owners that is an executive or administrative assistant first, then support, bookkeeping, or sales support depending on where the bottleneck bites hardest.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>I tried a freelancer before and it did not work. Is this different? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Usually, yes. Most freelance failures trace back to no vetting, no work test, no documented processes, and a freelancer splitting attention across clients. A dedicated professional is recruited for your role, tested on real work, employed full-time for you only, and covered by a replacement guarantee.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How fast can a dedicated remote professional start? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">About 5 weeks from the first call to a fully onboarded professional, covering role design, sourcing, screening, your interviews, and a structured first month.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What does it cost to start? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">One monthly rate per professional: $1,500 for Associates, $2,500 for Professionals, from $5,000 for Experts. Recruitment is included, with no placement fees.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

